ed after 1964. Points were awarded in each race based on placement in the race and the number of boats racing. The worst of a boat’s seven scores were eliminated, thus using the best six of seven scores for the final total."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Only eight nations won yachting medals in 1964, led by the United States with five, although it did not win a gold medal, as five different nations won the five events. Denmark, Germany, and Sweden also won two medals."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9733"} "One Person Dinghy (Finn), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 21 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9746"} "Two Person Keelboat (Star), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 21 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "34"] "\n" [:td {} "17"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9772"} "Three Person Keelboat (Dragon), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 21 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "70"] "\n" [:td {} "23"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9759"} "Two Person Heavyweight Dinghy (Flying Dutchman), Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 21 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "42"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9785"} "5.5 metres, Open"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 21 October 1964"] "\n" [:td {} "46"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n225 (224/1)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n40 (40/1)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medals"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {:cols